; Reversing a string of letters, Metcalfe's first use of the editor:
;
;   <string> ::= <letter> K  J{ <letter> K X C }
;
; K is COPY, the integral sign J is "any number of times". For PQRS the
; output tape holds P Q X C R X C S X C, and the editor's stack ends as
; SRQP. Then EDIT W writes it.

        CALL    STRING
        EDIT    W
        STOP
STRING  CALL    LETTER
        FALSE   L1
        COPY
L3      CALL    LETTER
        FALSE   L2
        COPY
        EDIT    X
        EDIT    C
        TRUE    L3
L2      FLAG
L1      RETURN
LETTER  MATCH   P
        TRUE    T9
        MATCH   Q
        TRUE    T9
        MATCH   R
        TRUE    T9
        MATCH   S
T9      RETURN
